  <div class="case-body">

    <div class="case-section">
      <div class="case-section-title">Overview <span>/ The project</span></div>
      <p class="case-p">CareerChoice is a bilingual, visual-first career discovery platform designed for rural students and their families. It helps students explore, understand, compare, and choose career paths with clarity and confidence — bridging the gap between aspiration and information.</p>
      <div class="case-mockup-full">Mockup — Full App Preview</div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-section">
      <div class="case-section-title">The Problem <span>/ Why this matters</span></div>
      <p class="case-p">Rural students in India face serious career decision barriers that go beyond just lack of information. The problem is systemic — rooted in language, exposure, emotional pressure, and access.</p>
      <div class="case-grid">
        <div class="case-card">
          <div class="case-card-icon">🌐</div>
          <div class="case-card-title">Language Barrier</div>
          <div class="case-card-text">Most career platforms are English-first, making them inaccessible to Telugu-medium and low-literacy students.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-card">
          <div class="case-card-icon">👁</div>
          <div class="case-card-title">Limited Exposure</div>
          <div class="case-card-text">Students often know only 5–6 traditional careers — doctor, engineer, teacher — severely narrowing their choices.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-card">
          <div class="case-card-icon">💔</div>
          <div class="case-card-title">Emotional Pressure</div>
          <div class="case-card-text">60% face parental pressure. Fear, confusion, and lack of validation make decision-making deeply stressful.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-section">
      <div class="case-section-title">Research Insights <span>/ What the data revealed</span></div>
      <div class="case-stat-row">
        <div class="case-stat">
          <div class="case-stat-num">70%</div>
          <div class="case-stat-label">Know only 5–6 traditional careers</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-stat">
          <div class="case-stat-num">41%</div>
          <div class="case-stat-label">Report confusion and fear</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-stat">
          <div class="case-stat-num">80%</div>
          <div class="case-stat-label">Parents have low modern career exposure</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-stat">
          <div class="case-stat-num">86%</div>
          <div class="case-stat-label">Prefer visual content over text</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="case-p">Research process spanned literature review, surveys, interviews, contextual observations, prior art analysis, thematic analysis, and usability testing — building a thorough understanding of the real barriers students face.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="case-section">
      <div class="case-section-title">Target Users <span>/ Who this is for</span></div>
      <div class="case-grid case-grid-2">
        <div class="case-card">
          <div class="case-card-title">Primary Users</div>
          <div class="case-card-text">Rural students aged 14–20, Telugu-medium and low-literacy students, and parents with limited digital literacy.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-card">
          <div class="case-card-title">Secondary Users</div>
          <div class="case-card-text">Government school teachers, NGOs working in education, and career development organizations.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-section">
      <div class="case-section-title">Design Gap <span>/ What existing platforms miss</span></div>
      <p class="case-p">Existing career platforms are built for urban, English-literate users. They fail rural students in nearly every dimension.</p>
      <div class="case-tags-wrap">
        <span class="case-tag">Text-heavy</span>
        <span class="case-tag">English-first</span>
        <span class="case-tag">Assessment-gated</span>
        <span class="case-tag">Urban-focused</span>
        <span class="case-tag">Weak emotional guidance</span>
        <span class="case-tag">No parent involvement</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="case-section">
      <div class="case-section-title">The Solution <span>/ CareerChoice</span></div>
      <p class="case-p">CareerChoice flips the paradigm — visual-first, bilingual by design, and built around emotional safety and family involvement.</p>
      <div class="case-features">
        <div class="case-feature">
          <div class="case-feature-dot"></div>
          <div><div class="case-feature-title">Visual Career Cards</div><div class="case-feature-text">300+ richly illustrated cards that explain careers without walls of text.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-feature">
          <div class="case-feature-dot"></div>
          <div><div class="case-feature-title">Telugu + English Interface</div><div class="case-feature-text">Seamless bilingual toggle so students can learn in the language they're most comfortable in.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-feature">
          <div class="case-feature-dot"></div>
          <div><div class="case-feature-title">Career Interest Test</div><div class="case-feature-text">45-question personalized assessment surfacing the right career paths for each student.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-feature">
          <div class="case-feature-dot"></div>
          <div><div class="case-feature-title">Career Comparison</div><div class="case-feature-text">Side-by-side comparison of salary, skills, education pathways, and responsibilities.</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="case-feature">
          <div class="case-feature-dot"></div>
          <div><div class="case-feature-title">Save & Shortlist</div><div class="case-feature-text">Students can bookmark and revisit options as their thinking evolves.</div></div>
